1
00:00:01,575 --> 00:00:03,635
Last time, we counted legs.

2
00:00:03,905 --> 00:00:05,285
Insects have six.

3
00:00:05,555 --> 00:00:08,665
And we met the reptiles, with dry, scaly skin.

4
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:10,055
Like Basil!

5
00:00:10,108 --> 00:00:11,628
Cold-blooded, and proud!

6
00:00:13,443 --> 00:00:14,773
Today you'll learn...

7
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:16,460
How to spot a mammal.

8
00:00:16,627 --> 00:00:18,347
Which one does not belong.

9
00:00:18,515 --> 00:00:20,665
Same and different, with a reason.

10
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:22,690
Lock in first.

11
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:25,460
A little animal is hiding in this video.

12
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:26,950
Can you spot it?

13
00:00:30,263 --> 00:00:31,143
Round one.

14
00:00:31,443 --> 00:00:33,053
This animal has wings.

15
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:34,333
It flies.

16
00:00:34,613 --> 00:00:35,823
Is a bat a bird?

17
00:00:36,143 --> 00:00:37,223
One, yes.

18
00:00:37,493 --> 00:00:38,353
Two, no.

19
00:00:38,643 --> 00:00:40,123
Show me with your fingers.

20
00:00:45,588 --> 00:00:46,568
Locked in!

21
00:00:46,696 --> 00:00:47,316
One!

22
00:00:47,456 --> 00:00:48,906
It flies, like a bird!

23
00:00:48,957 --> 00:00:49,717
Two!

24
00:00:49,807 --> 00:00:51,367
I think I see fur.

25
00:00:51,413 --> 00:00:52,203
Two.

26
00:00:52,473 --> 00:00:53,693
No feathers.

27
00:00:54,115 --> 00:00:54,995
Be a hair!

28
00:00:55,285 --> 00:00:56,265
Shrink down.

29
00:00:56,545 --> 00:00:57,475
Quietly.

30
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:01,953
You are one hair on a fruit bat's back.

31
00:01:02,436 --> 00:01:05,220
Soft fur, like a forest, all around you.

32
00:01:05,785 --> 00:01:07,245
It spreads its wings.

33
00:01:07,695 --> 00:01:08,705
Thin skin.

34
00:01:09,145 --> 00:01:10,295
No feathers!

35
00:01:10,883 --> 00:01:11,713
Whoosh!

36
00:01:12,193 --> 00:01:13,473
Out into the night.

37
00:01:13,893 --> 00:01:15,123
The air is cool.

38
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,543
But the body under you stays warm.

39
00:01:18,195 --> 00:01:21,765
Back at the palm, a baby bat drinks its mother's milk.

40
00:01:24,187 --> 00:01:25,497
The answer is two.

41
00:01:25,777 --> 00:01:27,257
A bat is not a bird.

42
00:01:27,547 --> 00:01:28,747
It is a mammal!

43
00:01:31,608 --> 00:01:32,638
Two fingers?

44
00:01:32,908 --> 00:01:34,128
One finger up!

45
00:01:34,176 --> 00:01:34,806
Fur!

46
00:01:34,976 --> 00:01:36,086
Not feathers!

47
00:01:36,508 --> 00:01:37,728
Say it with me!

48
00:01:38,441 --> 00:01:42,291
Mammals are animals that have hair or fur as their outer covering.

49
00:01:44,913 --> 00:01:47,013
Monkeys, cats, bats, and you!

50
00:01:47,283 --> 00:01:48,833
They all have hair or fur.

51
00:01:48,886 --> 00:01:50,426
Pip and I are mammals!

52
00:01:50,436 --> 00:01:51,706
And I'm the reptile.

53
00:01:51,826 --> 00:01:53,106
No fur for me!

54
00:01:53,452 --> 00:01:56,022
Most mammals give birth to their young alive.

55
00:01:56,302 --> 00:02:00,722
The females have mammary glands that can produce milk for their young.

56
00:02:03,938 --> 00:02:09,388
Mammals are warm-blooded, which means that they can maintain a constant body

57
00:02:09,138 --> 00:02:10,078
temperature.

58
00:02:14,202 --> 00:02:15,282
Exam tip!

59
00:02:15,572 --> 00:02:17,192
Compare a bat and a bird.

60
00:02:17,316 --> 00:02:20,556
A bat and a bird are similar because both have wings.

61
00:02:20,826 --> 00:02:23,976
They are different because a bat has fur, but a bird has

62
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:24,496
feathers.

63
00:02:26,015 --> 00:02:27,025
Round two.

64
00:02:27,305 --> 00:02:28,825
Which one does not belong?

65
00:02:29,125 --> 00:02:30,245
One, a cat.

66
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:31,705
Two, a monkey.

67
00:02:31,975 --> 00:02:33,275
Three, a lizard.

68
00:02:33,565 --> 00:02:35,045
Show me with your fingers.

69
00:02:40,515 --> 00:02:41,495
Locked in!

70
00:02:41,623 --> 00:02:42,513
Two.

71
00:02:42,643 --> 00:02:43,763
The monkey.

72
00:02:43,893 --> 00:02:45,343
It climbs trees.

73
00:02:45,392 --> 00:02:46,092
Three!

74
00:02:46,412 --> 00:02:47,442
No fur.

75
00:02:47,495 --> 00:02:48,195
Three!

76
00:02:48,325 --> 00:02:49,345
Like me!

77
00:02:49,542 --> 00:02:50,902
The answer is three.

78
00:02:51,192 --> 00:02:52,682
Find what the others share.

79
00:02:52,972 --> 00:02:55,642
A cat and a monkey have fur: mammals.

80
00:02:55,922 --> 00:02:59,152
A lizard has dry, scaly skin: a reptile.

81
00:02:59,202 --> 00:03:00,292
Three fingers?

82
00:03:00,562 --> 00:03:01,772
One finger up!

83
00:03:01,822 --> 00:03:02,462
Oops.

84
00:03:02,842 --> 00:03:04,282
Cats climb too!

85
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:05,490
Scales, not fur.

86
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:07,100
The odd one out is me!

87
00:03:08,599 --> 00:03:09,229
One.

88
00:03:08,979 --> 00:03:10,849
It has scaly skin.

89
00:03:10,989 --> 00:03:11,599
Two.

90
00:03:11,829 --> 00:03:13,659
It breathes air with its lungs.

91
00:03:13,709 --> 00:03:14,309
Three.

92
00:03:14,669 --> 00:03:16,959
It swims in the sea, so it is a fish!

93
00:03:17,236 --> 00:03:18,136
Showdown!

94
00:03:18,446 --> 00:03:19,576
Double points.

95
00:03:19,846 --> 00:03:21,466
One line has a mistake.

96
00:03:21,756 --> 00:03:23,516
Line one, two, or three?

97
00:03:23,816 --> 00:03:25,286
Show me with your fingers.

98
00:03:31,761 --> 00:03:32,741
Locked in!

99
00:03:32,869 --> 00:03:33,329
Three.

100
00:03:33,939 --> 00:03:36,129
Fish usually breathe through gills.

101
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:36,950
Three!

102
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,210
That's my group!

103
00:03:38,265 --> 00:03:38,875
Oops!

104
00:03:39,746 --> 00:03:41,096
Read all the clues.

105
00:03:41,376 --> 00:03:43,936
Scaly skin and lungs: a reptile.

106
00:03:44,296 --> 00:03:45,586
It is a sea turtle!

107
00:03:45,717 --> 00:03:47,077
Showed three fingers?

108
00:03:47,357 --> 00:03:49,257
Put up two more on your score hand!

109
00:03:49,309 --> 00:03:49,989
Fixed!

110
00:03:50,595 --> 00:03:52,125
Six animal groups!

111
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,021
Say it with us!

112
00:03:54,681 --> 00:03:55,591
Six legs?

113
00:03:55,561 --> 00:03:56,431
Insect!

114
00:03:58,281 --> 00:03:59,351
Dry, scaly skin?

115
00:03:59,161 --> 00:04:00,111
Reptile!

116
00:04:01,881 --> 00:04:02,791
Hair or fur?

117
00:04:02,761 --> 00:04:03,597
Mammal!

118
00:04:06,086 --> 00:04:07,236
Exam corner!

119
00:04:07,509 --> 00:04:08,809
Say it with me!

120
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:13,940
Living things such as plants and animals can be classified based on

121
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:16,000
common observable characteristics.

122
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,610
There are different types of plants and animals.

123
00:04:21,237 --> 00:04:22,707
Show me your score hand!

124
00:04:22,987 --> 00:04:24,017
More than two?

125
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,677
You beat the Buddies.

126
00:04:25,947 --> 00:04:27,057
Four fingers?

127
00:04:27,327 --> 00:04:28,337
High five!

128
00:04:28,842 --> 00:04:30,582
Did you spot the hidden animal?

129
00:04:30,872 --> 00:04:33,072
It was the squirrel, on the palm trunk!

130
00:04:33,372 --> 00:04:35,802
Is it cold-blooded, or warm-blooded?

131
00:04:36,072 --> 00:04:37,382
Tell someone at home.

132
00:04:38,264 --> 00:04:40,554
Next time: fungi and bacteria!

133
00:04:40,844 --> 00:04:42,054
Mould on bread.

134
00:04:42,354 --> 00:04:44,074
Yeast, for making bread.

135
00:04:44,344 --> 00:04:45,604
Both are fungi!

136
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:47,294
Which one is useful?

137
00:04:47,564 --> 00:04:48,884
Lock in your answer!

138
00:04:49,606 --> 00:04:51,806
Let's read today's key words together!

139
00:04:52,096 --> 00:04:52,856
Ready?

140
00:04:53,193 --> 00:04:53,920
Mammals.

141
00:04:55,407 --> 00:04:56,667
Mammary glands.

142
00:04:58,343 --> 00:04:59,373
Warm-blooded.

143
00:05:00,915 --> 00:05:01,855
Well done!

144
00:05:02,837 --> 00:05:03,941
Say it with us!

145
00:05:04,741 --> 00:05:05,491
Ready?

146
00:05:05,615 --> 00:05:06,275
One!

147
00:05:06,615 --> 00:05:07,315
two!

148
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,795
Now you know!
